{
  "name": "Catch Scope Creep with AI: Freelancer Change-Order Guard using Gmail, OpenAI and Google Sheets",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "02a8b7c4-1d41-42fe-b9cc-ed61dbd5bbbf",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1800,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 520,
        "height": 760,
        "content": "## Scope Creep Guard: AI Change-Order Assistant for Freelancers\n\nClients keep asking for \"one small extra\" and freelancers say yes to avoid awkward\nconversations, bleeding 30+ unbilled hours per project. This workflow watches your\ninbox, compares every client request against your agreed scope of work, and drafts\na warm-but-firm change-order email the moment a request falls outside the scope.\n\n### How it works\n1. The Gmail trigger fires on every new client email (press Execute on the manual\ntrigger any time to test with a sample).\n2. The Configuration node holds everything you edit once: your scope of work text,\nhourly rate, and where drafts and alerts go.\n3. AI reads the email against your scope and classifies it: in_scope, out_of_scope,\nor ambiguous, quoting the exact scope clause and estimating extra hours and cost.\n4. Out-of-scope requests get a ready-to-review change-order draft emailed to YOU\n(not the client). Ambiguous ones ping you on Telegram. In-scope ones are just logged.\n5. Every decision lands in a Google Sheets ledger so you always know how much\nunbilled work you quoted, waived, or are still owed.\n\n### Setup\n1. Paste your scope of work (or scope bullets) into the Configuration node.\n2. Set the Gmail trigger filter to your client, e.g. from:client@company.com.\n3. Connect Gmail, OpenAI, Google Sheets, and Telegram credentials.\n4. Create a blank Google Sheet and paste its ID into the Configuration node.\n\nNothing is ever sent to the client automatically. You always review first."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "cdef6811-9009-4f07-9daf-cfc3ef57116d",
      "name": "Section: Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1240,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "### 1 | Trigger\nEvery new client email starts the check. Use the manual trigger to test with a sample email."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
